<newsitem itemid="202250" id="root" date="1996-11-20" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Rhoex lifts yr shr, no div.</title>
<headline>Rhoex lifts yr shr, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     47.97	 vs   16.79</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  -	    vs    -</p>
<p>    Retained profit	 28.72	 vs   26.80</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   28.91	 vs   10.06</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    2.90	 vs    1.82</p>
<p>    Turnover		 110.18	 vs   47.29</p>
<p>Full name: Rhoex Ltd ((financial-mining holding)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the existing levels of profitability were expected to be sustained or improved, provided the current trend in the vanadium price and the value of the rand persisted during the remaining three months of the current financial period. It said the reduced interest burden would also have a positive effect.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
